{
  "id": "COMPOUND:43202 - PROTEIN:6153",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential mechanism by which 5H-Indolo[3,2-B]Quinolin-11(10H)-One interacts with Lysine-specific demethylase 4D-like. This compound is implicated in the target pathway through multiple routes, all leading to the same final target. The first pathway involves the compound directly targeting Dehydrogenase/reductase SDR family member 9, which in turn is a target of 5alpha,6alpha-Epoxy(22e,24r)-ergosta-8(14),22-dien-3beta,7alpha-diol and Dendridine A. These intermediates are all known to interact with Lysine-specific demethylase 4D-like, indicating a shared biological role in the pathway.\n\nThe evidence is consistent with a mechanism where 5H-Indolo[3,2-B]Quinolin-11(10H)-One acts as a modulator of a metabolic pathway that ultimately targets Lysine-specific demethylase 4D-like. The presence of multiple distinct intermediates that share the same target suggests that the compound may influence the activity of this enzyme in a broader context, possibly through a common downstream effect. The scores from the paths are comparable, indicating a strong and reliable relationship, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
